        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): ACP session startup fails when backend does not advertise thinking config",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen spawning an ACP session (e.g. OpenCode via `sessions_spawn(runtime: \"acp\")`), the Gateway injects model-level `thinking` defaults (from `agents.defaults.thinkingDefault`) into the ACP spawn options. The acpx wrapper translates `thinking` → `reasoning_effort` via `setConfigOption`, but the generic ACP manager rejects unadvertised keys *before* the wrapper runs. Backends that don't advertise `thinking` fail session startup.\n\n## Fix (3 commits, 2 files)\n\n**Commit 1 — `acp-spawn.ts`:** Stop auto-injecting model-level thinking defaults into ACP spawn options. Only explicit `thinkingOverride` (from agent config or spawn params) is passed through. This prevents the manager from trying to set `thinking`/`effort` on backends that don't support it.\n\n**Commit 2 — `runtime.ts`:** Forward the `getCapabilities` input handle to the delegate so session-scoped `configOptionKeys` (including `reasoning_effort`) are visible. Clone the array before injecting aliases to avoid mutating delegate-owned arrays.\n\n**Commit 3 — `runtime.ts` + tests:** Gate alias injection behind `isCodexAcpCommand`. The acpx `setConfigOption` only translates `thinking`/`thought_level` to `reasoning_effort` for Codex ACP sessions. Advertising aliases to non-Codex agents would claim support that doesn't exist.\n\n### Key design decision\n\nThe original approach (commit 3 of the first iteration) restored `resolveThinkingDefault` in `acp-spawn.ts`, reasoning that the capability normalization already solved the rejection. This was incorrect — backends like opencode that don't advertise `reasoning_effort` at all would still fail because the manager maps `thinking` → `effort` and the backend rejects it. The fix keeps `resolveThinkingDefault` removed so no thinking defaults are injected for backends that don't support them.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Forwards `getCapabilities` input handle\n- Injects aliases only when `reasoning_effort` is present\n- Confirms no `effort` alias injection (untranslated key)\n- Confirms non-mutation of delegate-owned arrays\n- Confirms no alias injection when `reasoning_effort` absent\n- Confirms no alias injection for non-Codex agents even when `reasoning_effort` is advertised\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nSee comment below — a real `sessions_spawn(runtime: \"acp\")` against opencode succeeded with `ACP_STARTUP_OK` after applying these changes.\n\nCloses #103802",
        "branch": "fix/acp-opencode-thinking-config",
